    "rgba(96,165,250,0.25)",
    "rgba(74,222,128,0.25)",
    "rgba(251,191,36,0.25)",
    "rgba(248,113,113,0.25)",
  ];

  /*
   * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   * HOW TO ADD A SONG TO THE COLLECTION
   * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   * Each song is an object with these fields:
   *
   *   name    — song title shown on the intro card
   *   artist  — artist / composer name
   *   year    — release or composition year (string, e.g. "1994" or "~1680")
   *   fact    — one fun/interesting fact shown on the intro card
   *   bpm     — tempo that controls tile fall speed:
   *               easy ≈ 60–80 · medium ≈ 90–120 · hard ≈ 130+
   *   notes   — array of [col, freq] pairs (see below)
   *
   * NOTES FORMAT:  [col, freq]
   *   col  — which of the 4 columns the tile appears in:
   *     0 (blue,  left):   lowest-pitch column
   *     1 (green):         mid-low pitch
   *     2 (yellow):        mid-high pitch
   *     3 (red,  right):   highest-pitch column
   *
   *   freq — audio frequency in Hz (used to play the note through Web Audio)
   *
   * FREQUENCY REFERENCE  (A4 = 440 Hz, equal temperament):
   *   C4=262  C#4=277  D4=294  Eb4=311  E4=330  F4=349  F#4=370
   *   G4=392  Ab4=415  A4=440  Bb4=466  B4=494  C5=523  C#5=554
   *   D5=587  Eb5=622  E5=659  F5=698   G5=784  A5=880
   *
   * COLUMN ASSIGNMENT GUIDE (assign based on relative pitch within the song):
   *   Map the lowest notes in your melody → col 0
   *   Map the highest notes                → col 3
   *   Spread the middle notes across col 1 and col 2
   *   Aim for a roughly even distribution across all 4 columns
   *   (uneven columns make one hand do all the work!)
   *
   * STEP-BY-STEP:
   *   1. Pick the most recognizable section (verse, chorus, or iconic riff).
   *   2. Hum or look up the melody note by note.
   *   3. Convert each note to Hz using the table above.
   *   4. Assign a col (0–3) based on relative pitch in your melody.
   *   5. Aim for 30–50 notes that loop cleanly back to the start.
   *   6. Set bpm to the natural feel — test by counting "1-2-3-4" to the song.
   *   7. Add the song to the correct difficulty array in SONGS below.
   * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   */
